course: dictionary
lesson: 14918
title: Referents: what a word points to
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A referent is the real thing, person or idea that a word points to. In «The dog barked loudly», the referent of «the dog» is the actual dog that is barking.
explain: Small words like «it», «she» and «they» are pronouns, and they point back to a referent that came earlier. In «Mia put her bag on the chair, and then she sat down», the referent of «she» is Mia.
explain: When it is not clear what a pronoun points to, the sentence confuses the reader. Good writers make the referent clear, sometimes by repeating the name instead of using a pronoun.
fact: A referent is the real thing, person or idea that a word points to.
fact: A pronoun such as «it», «she» or «they» refers back to its referent.
fact: An unclear referent makes a sentence confusing, because the reader cannot tell who or what is meant.
fact: In maths, «each» can have a referent too: in «Tom has 3 bags; each has 5 apples», «each» refers to the bags.
fact: Writers can fix an unclear referent by repeating the noun, for example writing «Ben» instead of «he».
exercise: In «Mia put her bag on the chair, and then she sat down», what is the referent of «she»? | The chair | Her bag | Nobody, because «she» is not a real word | *Mia
exercise: In «Tom has 3 bags; each has 5 apples», what does «each» refer to? | *The bags | The number 5 | The apples | Tom
exercise: Which word is a pronoun that points back to its referent? | Quickly | Happy | Table | *She
test: In «The rabbit ate the carrot because it was hungry», what is the referent of «it»? | *The rabbit | Hungry | The carrot | The garden
test: Which sentence has a clear referent for «it»? | *The rabbit ate the carrot, and the rabbit was happy. | The rabbit ate the carrot, and it ate the carrot. | The rabbit ate the carrot, and it was happy. | It was happy.
exam: What does referent mean? | *The real thing, person or idea that a word points to | A pronoun that is only used in maths | A sentence with no verb in it | A word that means the opposite of another word
